\import{macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{Preference-optimization objective}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{preference-optimization}
\tag{loss}

\p{A \strong{preference-optimization objective} is a functional of a policy
whose empirical terms compare the policy's treatment of #{y^+} and #{y^-}:
}

##{
 L_{\mathrm{pref}}(\theta)
 =\mathbb E_{(x,y^+,y^-)\sim\mathcal D_{\mathrm{pref}}}
   [\ell_\theta(x,y^+,y^-)].
}

\p{The comparison loss #{\ell_\theta} is part of the method. It may use a
learned reward, policy likelihoods, or a fixed comparison policy. Direct
Preference Optimization derives one such loss in
\citet{Section 4.1, especially Equation (7)}{rafailov2023direct}.}

\p{This definition names a family. It does not identify all preference
methods with DPO or with Bradley--Terry reward learning.}
